          "type": "tool_use",
          "name": "exec",
          "input": "const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-knowledge-issues/tracker.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Evolve the live, file-native Knowledge Space MVP into multi-space, indexed retrieval without making a database or index authoritative over the user's files.\\n+\\n+This is the follow-on tracker to #515. It is deliberately not a sub-issue of #515 and does not expand that tracker's current exit gate.\\n+\\n+## Architecture contract\\n+\\n+- Markdown files remain canonical; indexes and embeddings are disposable, node-local projections.\\n+- Reuse corpus-neutral primitives from #194 where they fit, but keep Knowledge tables, lifecycle, authorization, and freshness semantics separate from chat search.\\n+- Track file changes with watcher/Git signals for latency and periodic manifest reconciliation for correctness.\\n+- Chunk Markdown deterministically around semantic boundaries and retain path, heading path, line range, and source-content hash provenance.\\n+- Support lexical retrieval first; add embeddings only after the shared episodic embedding substrate exists; add hybrid fusion only after episodic hybrid retrieval establishes the shared mechanism.\\n+- Revalidate selected passages against the live file before returning them. Stale derived data must not become a citation authority.\\n+- Multiple spaces have stable identities. Display names are not identity. Equal IDs represent replicas; importing as a fork mints a new ID.\\n+- Derived indexes and embeddings never synchronize between personal Nodes; rebuild them locally from canonical files and portable metadata.\\n+\\n+## Child sequence\\n+\\n+1. Multiple Knowledge Spaces and stable Run bindings.\\n+2. Passage-oriented search results and ranged reads.\\n+3. Node-local Markdown chunk projection and lexical retrieval.\\n+4. Knowledge chunk embeddings on the shared search embedding substrate.\\n+5. Hybrid lexical/vector Knowledge retrieval.\\n+6. Portable Knowledge Space identity for import, fork, and replica semantics.\\n+\\n+Some work can proceed in parallel after its explicit blockers clear; this list is not a demand for one giant PR stack.\\n+\\n+## Non-goals\\n+\\n+- No remote filesystem mounting or arbitrary host filesystem access.\\n+- No synchronization of index rows or embedding vectors.\\n+- No requirement for approximate vector indexes, rerankers, OCR, non-text formats, or full Personal Realm synchronization in the first implementation.\\n+- No reuse of chat-search persistence tables as Knowledge persistence.\\n+\\n+## Related trackers\\n+\\n+- #515 — current file-native personal intelligence sequence and prerequisite MVP.\\n+- #194 — episodic-search tracker that owns shared embedding and hybrid-retrieval substrate.\\n+- #485 — merged product-direction record for local nodes and distributed personal state; reference only, not a dependency issue.\\n+\\n+## Exit criteria\\n+\\n+- Every child issue is closed or explicitly moved to a successor tracker with rationale.\\n+- Search results identify a stable space plus live-file provenance and remain usable for bounded follow-up reads.\\n+- Lexical retrieval works without an embedding provider; semantic retrieval degrades cleanly when embeddings are unavailable.\\n+- Cross-tenant access is denied in storage and service tests.\\n+- A local Node can rebuild all derived search state from canonical Knowledge files plus portable space metadata.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n",
