          "input": "const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-knowledge-issues/multi-space.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Allow one user to own and authorize multiple Knowledge Spaces without ambiguous names, cross-tenant leakage, or non-reproducible tool behavior during a Run.\\n+\\n+Parent: #541\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Replace the one-space-per-owner invariant with stable per-space IDs and owner-scoped records.\\n+- Keep display names user-editable and non-unique; identity and tool selection use stable IDs/opaque handles.\\n+- Define how a Chat chooses defaults and how a Run snapshots the authorized set so retries and worker execution do not silently search newly attached spaces.\\n+- Let Knowledge tools target one authorized space or the Run's authorized set without accepting a caller-supplied owner ID.\\n+- Preserve local-node operation: a personal node may omit redundant local `user_id` columns, while hub persistence remains RLS-enforced.\\n+- Define deletion/detachment behavior for queued and active Runs.\\n+\\n+## Design gate\\n+\\n+Choose the product binding contract before implementation. Recommended default: a Chat stores an editable default set; each Run persists the resolved space IDs and authorization revision. Dynamic \\\"all spaces I own\\\" lookup during execution is not reproducible and should not be the default.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- A user can create and address at least two spaces with the same display name and different IDs.\\n+- A Run sees only its persisted authorized space set across retries and worker handoff.\\n+- Another tenant cannot enumerate, bind, search, or read a space by guessing its ID.\\n+- Removing access fails closed for subsequent tool calls; queued/active-Run semantics are specified and tested.\\n+- Existing single-space installations migrate without changing the current space's identity.\\n+- API and database negative tests cover cross-tenant access.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- No import, replica, fork, or synchronization protocol here.\\n+- No indexing or embedding work.\\n+- No arbitrary host path supplied by a user or model.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-knowledge-issues/tool-v2.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Make Knowledge search return useful passages and make Knowledge reads bounded and addressable, without requiring an index.\\n+\\n+Parent: #541\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Change search results from one matching line per file to bounded passage results containing `knowledgeSpaceId`, path, heading path when available, start/end line, excerpt, file-content hash, and match mode.\\n+- Add ranged reads using a start line plus bounded line count (or an equivalent cursor contract).\\n+- Accept an optional expected file-content hash so an agent can detect that a search result became stale before reading it.\\n+- Define deterministic truncation, pagination/continuation, ordering, and errors for invalid ranges, changed files, oversized output, and deleted paths.\\n+- Preserve the configured-root, text-only, trusted-writer filesystem boundary from the live Knowledge MVP.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- Search returns bounded surrounding context rather than only the literal matching line.\\n+- Read can retrieve a bounded line range without buffering or returning the whole file.\\n+- A hash mismatch produces an explicit changed-content result; it never silently presents the new bytes as the old citation.\\n+- Results are deterministic for unchanged files and include enough provenance for a follow-up read.\\n+- Global file/entry/byte/output budgets and cooperative cancellation remain enforced.\\n+- Symlinks and paths outside the configured Knowledge root remain inaccessible.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- The implementation may still scan live files; no database index is required.\\n+- No embedding or semantic retrieval.\\n+- Line coordinates are navigation hints tied to a content hash, not permanent citations.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-knowledge-issues/lexical-index.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Build a disposable, node-local projection of live Markdown Knowledge files and use it for fast lexical passage retrieval.\\n+\\n+Parent: #541\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Reconcile configured Knowledge roots into per-space file and chunk projection rows.\\n+- Use deterministic Markdown-aware chunks based on headings, paragraphs, lists, and fenced-code boundaries, retaining path, heading path, line range, chunk ordinal, and source-content hash.\\n+- Normalize text consistently and support full-text plus trigram/fuzzy lexical candidates.\\n+- Treat filesystem/Git change signals as latency optimizations; use startup and periodic manifest reconciliation as the correctness mechanism for missed events, deletes, renames, and offline edits.\\n+- Atomically replace projection state for a changed file and garbage-collect deleted content.\\n+- Revalidate selected results against the live file/hash before returning them through the passage-search contract.\\n+- Keep all derived state local to the node and rebuildable.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- Initial indexing, incremental update, rename, deletion, missed-watcher-event, and full rebuild paths converge to the same projection.\\n+- Lexical queries rank exact, normalized, and fuzzy matches with deterministic tie-breaking.\\n+- A stale projection cannot return unverified old content as a live result.\\n+- Search remains available in a defined degraded mode while a projection is absent or rebuilding.\\n+- Projection rows are tenant/space isolated and covered by negative RLS/service tests.\\n+- Representative-vault benchmarks and relevance fixtures establish explicit latency and quality baselines before optimization.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- Files remain canonical; this issue does not create database-authored Knowledge content.\\n+- No embeddings, vector query, reranker, OCR, or non-text formats.\\n+- Do not reuse chat-search tables; reuse only corpus-neutral primitives where that reduces duplication.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-knowledge-issues/embeddings.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Embed Knowledge chunks using the provider, model-registry, batching, and lifecycle substrate established for episodic search, while keeping Knowledge projection state independent.\\n+\\n+Parent: #541\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Reuse the shared embedding model registry and corpus-neutral `EmbeddingBackend`/batch machinery delivered by #196.\\n+- Store vectors, model identity, chunk identity/hash, status, attempts, and retry metadata in Knowledge-owned projection tables.\\n+- Enqueue embeddings only for new or changed chunk hashes; delete or invalidate vectors when source chunks disappear.\\n+- Support model migration/re-embedding without making vectors canonical or blocking lexical search.\\n+- Define local-node behavior when the configured provider is unavailable or egress is disallowed.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- Unchanged chunks are not re-embedded during reconciliation.\\n+- Changed/deleted chunks cannot retain queryable stale vectors.\\n+- Embedding failures are retryable and observable while lexical retrieval remains available.\\n+- Switching the active Knowledge embedding model has an explicit backfill/cutover path.\\n+- Embedding jobs and vectors are tenant/space isolated.\\n+- A node can discard and rebuild all vectors from canonical files and local configuration.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- This issue prepares vector candidates; it does not expose semantic search to tools.\\n+- No synchronization of vectors between nodes.\\n+- No Knowledge-specific provider abstraction parallel to the shared search substrate.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-knowledge-issues/hybrid.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Retrieve Knowledge passages by exact wording, fuzzy wording, and paraphrased meaning through one bounded hybrid query path.\\n+\\n+Parent: #541\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Reuse the query-embedding and rank-fusion substrate established by episodic hybrid search in #197.\\n+- Generate lexical full-text/trigram and vector candidates from the same authorized space set.\\n+- Fuse candidates with deterministic reciprocal-rank fusion (or the shared equivalent), deduplicate chunk/file overlap, and return passage-oriented results.\\n+- Revalidate chosen passages against the live source hash before returning them.\\n+- Define explicit fallback when query embeddings, providers, or vector state are unavailable.\\n+- Add evaluation fixtures for exact terms, misspellings, paraphrases, cross-language queries where supported, stale files, and multi-space ambiguity.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- Paraphrase fixtures improve over lexical-only retrieval without materially regressing exact-match fixtures.\\n+- Lexical-only fallback is automatic and visible in result metadata when semantic retrieval is unavailable.\\n+- Candidate and output budgets are bounded; one large vault or space cannot starve the whole query.\\n+- Cross-tenant and unauthorized-space candidates are impossible at every retrieval stage.\\n+- Returned passages still match the live file hash or are rejected/refreshed before tool output.\\n+- Relevance and latency thresholds are recorded from a representative-vault benchmark.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- Start with exact pgvector search unless measured scale justifies ANN/HNSW.\\n+- No reranker until evaluation data demonstrates rank fusion is insufficient.\\n+- No chat/Knowledge cross-corpus result mixing in this issue.\\n*** Add File: /tmp/llame-knowledge-issues/portable-identity.md\\n+## Outcome\\n+\\n+Preserve Knowledge Space identity when files move between standalone and linked personal Nodes, while making replica and fork intent explicit.\\n+\\n+Parent: #541\\n+\\n+## Scope\\n+\\n+- Define a portable, versioned Knowledge Space manifest/envelope stored with or exported alongside canonical files.\\n+- Preserve a stable space ID across relocation and intentional replica import; display-name collisions do not merge spaces.\\n+- Support explicit import-as-fork that mints a new ID and records origin/lineage without rewriting source history.\\n+- Define collision behavior for same-ID imports with unrelated or divergent history; fail closed rather than silently merging.\\n+- Keep node-local mount/root configuration outside portable identity metadata.\\n+- Ensure derived indexes and embeddings are excluded from export/synchronization and rebuilt at the destination.\\n+- Integrate with Git-authored Knowledge writes from #212 without making Git commit identity the only space identity.\\n+\\n+## Acceptance criteria\\n+\\n+- Importing two different spaces with the same display name preserves both.\\n+- Importing the same space ID as a replica preserves identity and does not duplicate it accidentally.\\n+- Import-as-fork produces a distinct stable ID with inspectable origin metadata.\\n+- Same-ID incompatible content/history produces an explicit conflict requiring user choice.\\n+- Host paths, credentials, index rows, and embedding vectors are never included in the portable manifest.\\n+- The format is versioned, validated, and covered by malicious/corrupt-manifest tests.\\n+\\n+## Boundaries\\n+\\n+- No full Personal Realm synchronization engine, transport, or conflict-free file merge.\\n+- No automatic cloning or mounting on another machine.\\n+- No inference that equal names mean equal spaces.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n",
